      "content": "I hear you on the demographic shift, but \"predictable tactic\" and \"entrenched corporate interests\" feels like a pretty loaded way to describe the opposition. Doesn't that framing itself create a risk? If we adopt this super partisan tone, aren't we basically declaring ourselves an activist organization rather than a tech company? I'm worried we'd lose a massive chunk of our older, higher-income customers who just want us to focus on our products. Are you saying there's essentially no business case for staying neutral anymore?",
